## Artefact 2: ABC News Report (2024) – AI in Australian Workplaces

### Summary  
This 2024 ABC News segment examines how AI technologies are being introduced into Australian workplaces. The segment also highlights the benefits of its implementation such as increased efficiency, reduced administrative workload and improved data driven decision making. The report also discussed the risks of its implementation, including job displacement, algorithmic bias, privacy concerns and reduced human oversight. The segment also has a section on interviews with Australian workers and industry professionals, this section revealed mixed reactions with some viewing it as a productivity tool while others expressed concerns about fairness and transparency.



### Reflection  
I selected this artefact because it demonstrated the social impact of AI within local Australian contexts, which makes the topic more relevant to my future career. The segment also helped me understand how AI affects real people and how it influences job security, wellbeing and trust. The segment also highlighted the importance of transparency and fairness when deploying Ai systems in organisations. 

