## Artefact 3: Scholarly Article (2024) – Algorithmic Bias and Fairness

### Summary  
This 2024 article investigates how algorithmic bias continues to appear in modern Ai systems even when the system is trained on a large data sets. Through case studies involving facial recognition, hiring algorithms and predictive policing the authors have demonstrated biased data and flawed model designs can reinforce discrimination. The article also argues how technical fixes alone are not sufficient enough, calling for ethical frameworks and transparent auditing processes.

### Reflection  
I chose this article because it allowed me to engage with academic research. The article also helped me deepen my understanding of how bias emerges and why ICT professionals must make sure to critically evaluate datasets and model assumptions. It also reinforced idea about the limitations of purely technical solutions and the need for governance, transparency and human oversight. 
